## What landed

**Required-only permission snapshot** (`extensionbackgroundhost.cpp`): the gate source now reads `manifest.requiredPermissions` — `inspectManifest` merged `optional_permissions` into `permissions`, which would have let a declared-but-unconsented grant unlock gated APIs while `chrome.permissions.request` is still a typed `unsupported`.

**Backend namespace gates** (`extensionshimbackend.cpp`): the bridge object answers any code in the context, so absence from the shim's install list isn't a boundary. `storage`, `alarms`, `contextMenus`/`menus`, `sidePanel`, `sidebarAction` (manifest `sidebar_action` key), `notifications`, `idle`, and non-`getSelf` `management` members now answer typed `no-permission` when undeclared. `permissions.getAll`/`contains` report the granted set only.

**Per-frame host coverage** (`invokeScripting`): the page-level `agentCovers` only proved the top document — a covered page could frame an ungranted origin and `allFrames`/`frameIds` would inject into it. `collectFrames` now computes effective URLs (about:/empty inherit the embedder, `blob:` names its owning origin, data:/javascript: stay uncovered). Explicit uncovered `frameIds` reject the call; `allFrames` returns per-frame `no-host-access` entries. Shared by `executeScript`, `insertCSS`, `removeCSS`.

**Navigation gate** (`extensionNavUrl`): `tabs.create`/`tabs.update`/`windows.create` validate before touching UI — bundle-relative resolves onto the extension's own origin; foreign `chrome-extension://`, `javascript:`, `file:`/`qrc:` and traversal answer `url-refused`.

**Event scrub**: `pageUrl`/`frameUrl` join `url`/`title`/`favIconUrl` — a `contextMenus`-only extension still gets `onClicked` without learning where the click happened.

